Q: Query to calculate %diff. between two rows on two tables MYSQL A: <p>I would use a join.</p>
<p>Example:</p>
<pre><code>CREATE TABLE pop2024 (
  country CHAR(2),
  population INT
);

INSERT INTO pop2024 VALUES ('US', 340110988);

CREATE TABLE pop2025 (
  country CHAR(2),
  population INT
);

INSERT INTO pop2025 VALUES ('US', 341784857);

SELECT pop2025.population - pop2024.population AS population_difference
FROM pop2025 JOIN pop2024 USING (country);

+-----------------------+
| population_difference |
+-----------------------+
|               1673869 |
+-----------------------+
</code></pre>
<p>This is just an example to demonstrate the technique. If your tables are different than this example, you will have to adapt the solution.</p>
